# Text typed into a channel or query goes out as PRIVMSG and, without
# echo-message, is printed at once (Textual's `sendText:`). `//x` sends
# `/x` and a lone `/` is text. Textual sends to a parted channel too and
# lets the server answer. Offline the line is still printed, and the
# console says it was not sent. In the console every line is a command.
! welcome
< :textual!u@h JOIN #c
> MODE #c
! type #c hi all
> PRIVMSG #c :hi all
? line #c <textual> hi all
? unread #c 0 highlights 0
! type #c //notacommand
> PRIVMSG #c /notacommand
? line #c <textual> /notacommand
! type #c /
> PRIVMSG #c /
? line #c <textual> /
! type console hello there
> HELLO there
< :textual!u@h PART #c
! type #c anyone?
> PRIVMSG #c anyone?
? line #c <textual> anyone?
! disconnect
> QUIT
< ERROR :Closing Link
> hangup #1
? notice Disconnected: quit
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG textual :late
! type #c x
? line #c <textual> x
? notice Failed to send data to server. Not connected.
? offline user-quit
